-- Passage rg9-argument-evidence-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('246e0f16-a078-574b-9ec5-789814524639', 'rg9-argument-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-argument-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Light Up the Square on Summer Nights$q$, $q$Every summer evening, downtown Marlow goes quiet by six o'clock. The shops close, the sidewalks empty, and the town square sits unused until morning. The town should host a weekly night market in the square from June through August.

A night market would help local businesses. Vendors could sell food, crafts and produce, and nearby shops could stay open later to catch the crowds. In Ridgeport, a town about the size of Marlow, shop owners near the night market reported that their Friday sales rose by an average of twenty percent during the market's first summer.

The market would also give families a place to gather. Many residents work during the day and cannot visit the Saturday farmers market, so an evening event would fit their schedules.

Some people complain that a night market would bring noise. But the market would end at ten o'clock, and the square is surrounded mostly by shops and offices, not homes. Only two apartment buildings face the square directly.

Critics also say the town cannot afford to pay for extra trash pickup and safety staff. Ridgeport covered these costs by charging each vendor a weekly fee of forty dollars, and the fees paid for every expense in the first year.

We have a simple choice. Either we host a night market, or downtown Marlow will slowly die. If we turn down this idea, shops will close one by one, and soon the square will be empty forever.

Summer nights are too valuable to waste. Let's fill the square with lights, music and neighbors.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
