   $q$Why does the author mention that Ridgeport is about the size of Marlow?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To make the results from Ridgeport seem more likely to apply to Marlow.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To prove that every town of that size should hold a night market.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"To show that Ridgeport and Marlow compete for the same shoppers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To explain why Ridgeport's shops close at six o'clock each night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To make the results from Ridgeport seem more likely to apply to Marlow.$q$, $q$Evidence from another town is more relevant when that town is similar, so the size detail strengthens the comparison. It does not prove that every town of that size must hold a market.$q$, 'draft', '246e0f16-a078-574b-9ec5-789814524639')
