   $q$Which of the author's reasons is supported with the least evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Noise from the market would not disturb many residents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overlooks-evidence"},{"text":"Vendor fees could cover the costs of trash pickup and staff.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overlooks-evidence"},{"text":"The market would give working families a place to gather.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The market would help local businesses increase their sales.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overlooks-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The market would give working families a place to gather.$q$, $q$The claim about families rests only on the statement that many residents work during the day, with no survey or numbers. Sales, noise and cost are each backed by specific facts such as Ridgeport's twenty percent rise.$q$, 'draft', '246e0f16-a078-574b-9ec5-789814524639')
