   $q$According to the passage, which of Mr. Adeyemi's claims is supported by measured evidence that relates directly to it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Students were more active with the standing desks.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students focused better with the standing desks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"accepts-weak-evidence"},{"text":"Standing desks will improve health across the school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"accepts-weak-evidence"},{"text":"Every classroom in the school should get new desks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-claim-for-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Students were more active with the standing desks.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says the step counts are "directly related to the claim" and "measured rather than guessed." The test scores for the focus claim are described as weak evidence.$q$, 'draft', '21e450e6-d9b0-54da-801e-e62e3cdee874')
